<title>PORTUGAL: Yield eases on Portuguese three month bills.</title>
<headline>Yield eases on Portuguese three month bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield eased to 6.2327 percent, from 6.2678 percent previously, at the Treasury's sale of three month bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Treasury placed 20.5 billion escudos. The offer was 20 billion. The last such sale was on December 19.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
